Labnet change to validation.cpp for Bitcoin Knots v29.4.knots20260508.

ContextualCheckBlockHeader() skips the bad-diffbits check when
fPowNoRetargeting is set. Unlike the Core node, Knots keeps the IBD check
because it does not serve block templates.

--- a/src/validation.cpp
+++ b/src/validation.cpp
@@ -4597,7 +4597,8 @@
 
     // Check proof of work
     const Consensus::Params& consensusParams = chainman.GetConsensus();
-    if (block.nBits != GetNextWorkRequired(pindexPrev, &block, consensusParams))
+    // Without retargeting the Labnet accepts any nBits within powLimit
+    if (!consensusParams.fPowNoRetargeting && block.nBits != GetNextWorkRequired(pindexPrev, &block, consensusParams))
         return state.Invalid(BlockValidationResult::BLOCK_INVALID_HEADER, "bad-diffbits", "incorrect proof of work");
 
     // Check against checkpoints
